# What the hook component keeps out of the repository.
#
# The root .gitignore already excludes *.dll and *.exe everywhere, which covers out/ by accident of
# extension -- but not the object files, the generated build logs, the size probe's output, or the
# intermediate directories. Those are all regenerable from the sources, and a stale one in the tree
# is a way to debug a build that is not the one being compiled.
obj/
out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The PRIVATE auto-farmer module (`PLAN-AUTOFARM.md` section 13).
#
# The farmer's decision code is not published. `managed/Drelay.Bootstrap/Farmer.cs` is the public
# stub -- the same class surface with no behaviour -- and this directory is where the real module
# lives: `build.ps1` and both project files compile `private/**/*.cs` INSTEAD OF the stub when it
# is present, so dropping the file in is the whole installation.
#
# IGNORING THE DIRECTORY IS THE MECHANISM, NOT A CONVENIENCE. A checkout of this repository must
# never contain the module; a release of this component is built from a checkout, so a released
# `Drelay.Bootstrap.dll` is the stub build by construction. If `private/` ever shows up in
# `git status`, this rule has been broken and the module is one commit away from being published.
# Anchored (`/private/`) rather than a bare `private/`, so a directory of that name anywhere else
# in the tree is not silently ignored; this is one path and it is at the hook's root.
/private/

# The managed projects' `bin/Release` output.  It used to be covered by the root .gitignore's
# `*.dll` / `*.exe` lines, which are not in this tree any more -- and those lines never covered the
# `deps.json` / `runtimeconfig.json` / `.pdb` files beside them, so a sweep of this directory picked
# up eighteen build outputs and no sources were missing until someone tried to build from the
# commit.
bin/

# The linker's shared PDB, which cl.exe drops in the current directory of the batch file rather than
# beside the objects. It is regenerated on every build and is not a source.
vc140.pdb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated and third-party research inputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The full IL dump of the game assembly: an ~85 MB artifact regenerated from the installed build
# with ilspycmd. It is evidence -- tools/il_index.py cross-checks every pinned target against it and
# the documents under docs/hook/ cite it -- but it is derived from the shipped assembly rather than
# written by this project, and it is not versioned here. docs/hook/HOOK-BUILD-MATRIX.md records the
# procedure that reproduces it.
il/*
!il/.gitkeep

# The hook's scratch: per-run decision dumps, cost tables, trace files and probe output. Regenerable
# with the tooling in tools/ (Capture-DodgeDecisions.ps1, the SolverHarness), and never the evidence
# itself -- the numbers that matter are quoted into the reports under docs/hook/, which ARE tracked.
work/

# Local tool installs (ilspycmd and friends) and the string dumps taken from the game assembly.
# Both are regenerable and belong to no build.
.tools/
.dnscan/

# Commit-message scratch.
.commitmsg

# The release packaging directory written by the release workflow.
/dist/
